WEBVTT

00:00:03.330 --> 00:00:07.000
In a federated data space, each
practice, chain,

00:00:07.050 --> 00:00:12.220
insurer or payer keeps its records in its
own practice management software.

00:00:12.270 --> 00:00:15.400
A connector is installed next
to that software.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.920
The connector publishes in a
common catalogue

00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.800
which data exist, but not the
data themselves.

00:00:21.850 --> 00:00:26.160
When someone needs an indicator, the
question travels to each practice,

00:00:26.210 --> 00:00:30.560
is computed there, and only the
aggregated result comes back.

00:00:30.610 --> 00:00:35.040
Consents, metadata and results
move over the network.

00:00:35.090 --> 00:00:37.640
Never an identifiable record.

00:00:37.690 --> 00:00:40.020
The data stay in the practice.

00:00:40.070 --> 00:00:42.610
What travels is the answer.
